HST Office: Office-style drawing of the ribbon buttons and tabs, the same on Windows, macOS and Linux.

Owner decision (2026-11-07): owner-draw painting ships on for all three platforms; the OwnerDraw switch
(org.openoffice.Office.HSTRibbon, hst-ribbon-switches.patch) is rollback safety only.

Scoped to the Tabbed notebookbar: dialogs, the sidebar and classic toolbars keep the native theme.
High contrast always uses the native theme and the system colours. LibreOfficeKit is unchanged.
Colours are the tokens of docs/design/ribbon-look/PROPOSAL.md, light and dark.

- include/vcl/HstRibbonPaint.hxx, vcl/source/control/HstRibbonPaint.cxx (new): the palette, the
  high-contrast rule, the switch (read once per process), SetOwnerDraw() for a toolbox, and the
  button and tab painters. Buttons: rounded (3 px) hover fill; pressed stronger than checked;
  checked is a fill with an even 1 px border on all four sides; disabled draws no state. Tabs: no
  box; a light rounded fill on hover; the selected tab has a 2 px accent bar under its label.
- vcl/inc/toolbox.h, vcl/source/window/toolbox.cxx: ToolBox::ImplDrawButton draws with the palette
  when the toolbox is marked; control items (combo boxes) stay native.
- vcl/source/control/tabctrl.cxx: TabControl::ImplDrawItem draws notebookbar tabs with the palette;
  labels, the contextual tab marker and other tab controls are unchanged.
- sfx2/source/sidebar/SidebarToolBox.cxx: NotebookbarToolBox marks itself.
- vcl/Library_vcl.mk: builds HstRibbonPaint.

